2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Download More Movies, Series, and Dramas at
THENKIRI.COM

3
00:01:29,708 --> 00:01:32,166
You're my first catch in days, but

4
00:01:32,791 --> 00:01:34,000
you're too little.

5
00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:39,666
Whoa, look what's coming.

6
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:42,165
That one looks nasty.

7
00:01:42,166 --> 00:01:43,999
Yeah, it does.

8
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,083
I better get home before it hits.

9
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:48,625
- See you tomorrow.
- So long.

10
00:01:58,083 --> 00:02:02,583
<i>Everyone remembers where they were
the day the rain came.</i>

11
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:08,000
<i>It was a Sunday, not quite winter.</i>

12
00:02:09,166 --> 00:02:11,791
<i>The forecast had called for sun.</i>

13
00:02:13,708 --> 00:02:16,624
<i>This low-pressure system
offshore has turned</i>

14
00:02:16,625 --> 00:02:18,540
<i>and is moving in fast.</i>

15
00:02:18,541 --> 00:02:21,415
<i>Expect periods of
heavy rain showers across the city today,</i>

16
00:02:21,416 --> 00:02:23,665
<i>with winds gusting up to 30 miles per hour</i>

17
00:02:23,666 --> 00:02:27,124
{\an8}<i>and the threat
of minor coastal flooding and high surf.</i>

18
00:02:27,125 --> 00:02:29,415
{\an8}<i>The holidays are a month away,</i>

19
00:02:29,416 --> 00:02:32,707
<i>and hopefully,
the surprise turn in the weather will…</i>

20
00:02:32,708 --> 00:02:35,582
<i>People went about their mornings as usual.</i>

21
00:02:35,583 --> 00:02:37,457
{\an8}- Ready?
- Yeah, let's do it.

22
00:02:37,458 --> 00:02:39,500
{\an8}<i>We lived close to each other then…</i>

23
00:02:40,041 --> 00:02:41,624
{\an8}Okay, bye.

24
00:02:41,625 --> 00:02:44,583
{\an8}<i>…but it was easy to feel alone.</i>

25
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:49,082
{\an8}Guys, come on. It's gonna rain.

26
00:02:49,083 --> 00:02:50,458
{\an8}Yeah, let's go inside.

27
00:02:51,625 --> 00:02:53,125
<i>The day the rain came,</i>

28
00:02:54,041 --> 00:02:55,125
<i>we learned</i>

29
00:02:55,625 --> 00:02:57,208
<i>we were not alone.</i>

30
00:03:02,875 --> 00:03:05,499
<i>Last December was the warmest on record</i>

31
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:08,333
<i>for western Washington,
so keep tuned in for updates.</i>

32
00:03:18,666 --> 00:03:20,958
Come on. Come on.

33
00:03:36,208 --> 00:03:39,500
<i>And we learned just how far some will go</i>

34
00:03:40,375 --> 00:03:42,375
<i>to protect their home.</i>

35
00:04:02,291 --> 00:04:05,832
Hey, where is everybody?

36
00:04:05,833 --> 00:04:07,333
Where is everybody?

37
00:04:08,041 --> 00:04:10,416
There's my old boy.

38
00:04:21,333 --> 00:04:22,416
Good morning.

39
00:04:25,125 --> 00:04:28,749
- I can't believe the kids let me sleep in.
- Was wondering why it was so quiet.

40
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:30,249
You caught us breakfast?

41
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:32,750
Oh yeah. Big catch this morning.

42
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:36,082
World's best fisherman.

43
00:04:36,083 --> 00:04:37,583
- I know.
- Thank you.

44
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,291
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

45
00:04:40,875 --> 00:04:41,957
- Wake up!
- Donuts!

46
00:04:41,958 --> 00:04:43,124
- Whoa!
- Donuts!

47
00:04:43,125 --> 00:04:45,082
- Gimme.
- Can we make bacon?

48
00:04:45,083 --> 00:04:47,415
- Just calm down. Just… Come on.
- Bacon!

49
00:04:47,416 --> 00:04:49,624
- Please leave some for us!
- Vultures.

50
00:04:49,625 --> 00:04:51,290
- Total vultures.
- Turn it on!

51
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,457
- Okay.
- Make it work.

52
00:04:52,458 --> 00:04:55,707
I just gave Cassidy his meds,
and don't feed him any bacon.

53
00:04:55,708 --> 00:04:57,291
You deserve it more than they do.

54
00:05:00,625 --> 00:05:03,332
Dad, the streaming stopped working.

55
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:06,707
I don't know. I think
this house is really falling apart.

56
00:05:06,708 --> 00:05:08,332
- I'm ready to move when you are.
- Sure.

57
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:10,540
A few more lottery tickets
and we should be good to go.

58
00:05:10,541 --> 00:05:11,458
Hey.

59
00:05:13,125 --> 00:05:15,458
You know I'm just kidding, right?

60
00:05:15,958 --> 00:05:18,000
This isn't all on you.

61
00:05:20,583 --> 00:05:24,583
Oh, the guy is coming tomorrow
to check the cracks in the chimney.

62
00:05:25,083 --> 00:05:26,083
Mm.

63
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:28,874
- This is new.
- What?

64
00:05:28,875 --> 00:05:30,749
He thinks our foundation is sinking,

65
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:33,415
so the only thing
holding the house together is the chimney.

66
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:36,583
The house collapsing on us
while we're sleeping would be a bummer.

67
00:05:37,541 --> 00:05:39,332
Do you still wanna go buy
a Christmas tree?

68
00:05:39,333 --> 00:05:41,040
- It's raining out there.
- Come on.

69
00:05:41,041 --> 00:05:43,124
Wait, wait. Dad, come on.
You promised. Please.

70
00:05:43,125 --> 00:05:45,457
- I didn't promise. You promised.
- Dad!

71
00:05:45,458 --> 00:05:46,874
- You promised.
- Dad!

72
00:05:46,875 --> 00:05:48,375
- Who promised you guys?
- You!

73
00:05:49,541 --> 00:05:51,540
- Yeah, let's go.
- Come on.

74
00:05:51,541 --> 00:05:52,624
Let's buy a tree.

75
00:05:52,625 --> 00:05:54,083
- Let's go!
- I wanna pick!

76
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,082
- Help me put my shoes on.
- You know how to put your shoes on.

77
00:05:59,083 --> 00:06:00,749
Hey, no scooter in the house.

78
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:02,540
Come on, Mom! Let's go!

79
00:06:02,541 --> 00:06:06,082
- She always takes forever.
- Then you shouldn't act surprised, right?

80
00:06:06,083 --> 00:06:08,833
Help your sister put her shoes on.
Go wait in the car.

81
00:06:09,458 --> 00:06:10,708
Ann! Let's go!

82
00:06:11,375 --> 00:06:13,290
- Don't rush me.
- I'm not.

83
00:06:13,291 --> 00:06:15,457
I'm hiding from our children.

84
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:18,040
Seriously, when can we stop doing
this tree thing?

85
00:06:18,041 --> 00:06:19,875
It's Christmas, you Grinch.

86
00:06:21,791 --> 00:06:23,165
Okay, what did you do?

87
00:06:23,166 --> 00:06:24,665
You have to unlock it, stupid.

88
00:06:24,666 --> 00:06:26,374
- I did, stupid!
- Shut up!

89
00:06:26,375 --> 00:06:28,624
Stop arguing! You're both stupid.

90
00:06:28,625 --> 00:06:30,290
It won't open because of Graham.

91
00:06:30,291 --> 00:06:33,332
- Don't blame me. That was you.
- You obviously did something!

92
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:35,666
No, I didn't.
Why do you blame me all the time?

93
00:06:38,083 --> 00:06:39,415
It's <i>all</i> your fault!

94
00:06:39,416 --> 00:06:41,874
This is why <i>I'm</i> the favorite,
and you always cause problems.

95
00:06:41,875 --> 00:06:44,832
- Shut up. You're such a baby.
- I'm not a baby!

96
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:46,541
I'm 8 years old!

97
00:06:50,333 --> 00:06:51,790
What did you two do?

98
00:06:51,791 --> 00:06:53,375
- Nothing!
- Ugh!

99
00:06:59,166 --> 00:07:01,749
Quiet, Cass.

100
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:03,790
Okay, Cass, shush.

101
00:07:03,791 --> 00:07:05,665
Guys. Why aren't you in the car?

102
00:07:05,666 --> 00:07:07,249
- Door won't open.
- Can't get out.

103
00:07:07,250 --> 00:07:09,915
We've tried every door. Nothing will open.

104
00:07:09,916 --> 00:07:12,458
- You guys. Guys.
- I'll try the windows in my room.

105
00:07:25,625 --> 00:07:27,791
What? Okay.

106
00:07:44,291 --> 00:07:45,666
This is absurd.

107
00:07:53,958 --> 00:07:56,415
Yeah. It's a prank. Teenagers.

108
00:07:56,416 --> 00:08:00,124
They glued all the windows and doors shut
or something, right?

109
00:08:00,125 --> 00:08:02,332
No prank. Quiet, Cass!

110
00:08:02,333 --> 00:08:04,041
But I don't have any service.

111
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,999
Not connected. No Wi-Fi.

112
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Unplug the router
and plug it back in. D'you try that?

113
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:13,082
- Did you pay the bill?
- Yes.

114
00:08:13,083 --> 00:08:14,332
Cass, quiet!

115
00:08:14,333 --> 00:08:15,749
Do you have signal now?

116
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:17,540
- No, nothing.
- Mom, Dad.

117
00:08:17,541 --> 00:08:19,582
I tried the windows in my room.
Nothing's working.

118
00:08:19,583 --> 00:08:21,999
- It's like it's glued shut.
- Every window in there is stuck.

119
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,250
Cass!

120
00:08:32,250 --> 00:08:33,332
- Dad!
- Dad.

121
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:34,457
Are you okay?

122
00:08:34,458 --> 00:08:36,082
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

123
00:08:36,083 --> 00:08:37,458
Yeah, I'm fine.

124
00:08:39,333 --> 00:08:41,332
- I'm fine.
- Okay.

125
00:08:41,333 --> 00:08:42,708
What is going… Dad!

126
00:08:45,541 --> 00:08:47,249
- I don't understand.
- Okay, stand back.

127
00:08:47,250 --> 00:08:49,624
- Why? Wait. What are you talking about?
- Dad!

128
00:08:49,625 --> 00:08:51,624
- No, no!
- Stand back. I'll take care of this.

129
00:08:51,625 --> 00:08:52,750
Jason, no!

130
00:08:56,083 --> 00:08:57,583
- Just stop!
- Mom!

131
00:08:59,583 --> 00:09:01,500
- Stop!
- Dad!

132
00:09:08,083 --> 00:09:08,916
Mom.

133
00:09:16,250 --> 00:09:17,250
Dad.

134
00:09:28,458 --> 00:09:29,458
Kids.

135
00:09:34,583 --> 00:09:36,000
Dad, look!

136
00:09:41,291 --> 00:09:43,374
- Oh my God.
- It's not just us.

137
00:09:43,375 --> 00:09:45,874
- Hey, we can't get out.
- Look, someone's coming.

138
00:09:45,875 --> 00:09:46,916
Yeah.

139
00:09:47,416 --> 00:09:49,665
That's what's-her-name
from across the street.

140
00:09:49,666 --> 00:09:51,374
- Greg's wife.
- Whatever her name is.

141
00:09:51,375 --> 00:09:53,124
- Susan.
- Susan!

142
00:09:53,125 --> 00:09:55,040
Susan, go get help!

143
00:09:55,041 --> 00:09:57,291
We're stuck in here! Go get help!

144
00:09:58,083 --> 00:10:00,541
- He can't get out either.
- I'll be right back.

145
00:10:01,083 --> 00:10:02,915
Okay, okay, good. She's gonna go get help.

146
00:10:02,916 --> 00:10:04,666
- She's gonna go get help.
- Yeah.

147
00:10:05,458 --> 00:10:07,040
Great. It's okay.

148
00:10:07,041 --> 00:10:09,665
- So we're fine.
- Okay. Yeah. I know.

149
00:10:09,666 --> 00:10:11,790
It's… I…

150
00:10:11,791 --> 00:10:12,625
It's okay.

151
00:10:13,583 --> 00:10:15,083
Yeah, it's okay. Yeah.

152
00:10:43,041 --> 00:10:46,291
Okay, guys, let's see
what the neighbors are up to.

153
00:10:47,416 --> 00:10:49,582
- You know all the neighbors?
- Pretty much.

154
00:10:49,583 --> 00:10:52,290
Yeah, so the Richardsons are
across the street.

155
00:10:52,291 --> 00:10:54,665
They have three grandchildren,
and I think Max is a dentist.

156
00:10:54,666 --> 00:10:56,707
Yeah. That's what's-his-name.

157
00:10:56,708 --> 00:10:58,124
- Bike boy.
- Hmm?

158
00:10:58,125 --> 00:10:59,499
- Bike boy?
- Bike boy?

159
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,749
One of those guys
who wears all that dumb gear.

160
00:11:01,750 --> 00:11:04,207
It's Greg. His wife was the one
who ran to go get help.

161
00:11:04,208 --> 00:11:05,624
Why isn't she back yet?

162
00:11:05,625 --> 00:11:08,540
Don't worry. I'm sure
she'll be back with the police soon.

163
00:11:08,541 --> 00:11:10,333
Then there's that nosy guy down there.

164
00:11:11,208 --> 00:11:12,290
Oof.

165
00:11:12,291 --> 00:11:13,790
- What's his name?
- Oh my God.

166
00:11:13,791 --> 00:11:16,749
Do you know anyone's name here
on this street?

167
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:18,541
Yeah, this annoying lady with the dog.

168
00:11:19,750 --> 00:11:21,124
Who else?

169
00:11:21,125 --> 00:11:23,791
Oh, yeah. Let's not forget
doofus with the boat.

170
00:11:24,291 --> 00:11:25,540
What was it called?

171
00:11:25,541 --> 00:11:26,999
"Seas the Day"?

172
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,708
Such a doofus.

173
00:11:30,458 --> 00:11:31,791
- Good job.
- Mm-hmm.

174
00:11:34,833 --> 00:11:36,250
- Ann.
- Mm?

175
00:11:39,375 --> 00:11:41,374
"This was a one-night stand. LOL."

176
00:11:41,375 --> 00:11:43,249
Oh no!

177
00:11:43,250 --> 00:11:44,624
What's a one-night stand?

178
00:11:44,625 --> 00:11:46,415
- Um…
- It's an adult sleepover.

179
00:11:46,416 --> 00:11:48,665
What's the difference
between an adult sleepover

180
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:50,333
and a regular sleepover?

181
00:11:51,041 --> 00:11:54,707
Uh… Well, in an adult sleepover--

182
00:11:54,708 --> 00:11:57,415
- You can have as much candy as you want.
- That sounds fun.

183
00:11:57,416 --> 00:11:59,708
I guess so. I don't know.

184
00:12:02,875 --> 00:12:04,125
"Government?"

185
00:12:05,041 --> 00:12:06,249
Hey!

186
00:12:06,250 --> 00:12:07,999
That took a long time.

187
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,166
No, it didn't.

188
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:14,208
"Maybe. But why?"

189
00:12:18,083 --> 00:12:19,957
"For our safety?"

190
00:12:19,958 --> 00:12:22,666
Oh, look. Doofus with the boat has a sign.

191
00:12:23,666 --> 00:12:25,499
Is that how you spell aliens?

192
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:26,957
No, honey, it's not.

193
00:12:26,958 --> 00:12:29,249
Why would aliens wanna lock us all
in our houses?

194
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:30,750
They wouldn't, honey.

195
00:12:37,166 --> 00:12:38,416
"The whole world?"

196
00:12:50,041 --> 00:12:52,082
Okay, everybody, look at me.

197
00:12:52,083 --> 00:12:54,915
We are safe. We are in our home.

198
00:12:54,916 --> 00:12:58,708
We have everything we need here,
but most importantly, we have each other.

199
00:12:59,291 --> 00:13:02,291
- Can I have a donut?
- No. Eat your spaghetti.

200
00:13:02,791 --> 00:13:04,083
But I wanna stress eat.

201
00:13:04,750 --> 00:13:06,625
How do you know about stress eating, Ruth?

202
00:13:07,208 --> 00:13:08,416
Graham.

203
00:13:14,541 --> 00:13:17,875
If you can make it in there,
I can make it out here.

204
00:13:18,916 --> 00:13:21,665
Do you think
the running woman has found help?

205
00:13:21,666 --> 00:13:24,207
Someone's gonna come. I promise.

206
00:13:24,208 --> 00:13:26,041
I think it was the rain.

207
00:13:26,541 --> 00:13:28,166
The rain did this.

208
00:13:28,666 --> 00:13:31,625
No, baby, it's just rain.

209
00:13:33,333 --> 00:13:35,665
We'll be fine. I promise.

210
00:13:35,666 --> 00:13:38,625
The rain looked different today.

211
00:13:39,791 --> 00:13:42,083
I'm trying to keep it together
for the kids.

212
00:13:42,583 --> 00:13:46,040
But what the hell's going on, Jason?
How is this real? Like, honestly, how?

213
00:13:46,041 --> 00:13:48,624
- I don't know.
- Oh my God. My parents.

214
00:13:48,625 --> 00:13:50,624
They must be freaking out right now.

215
00:13:50,625 --> 00:13:53,165
The Richardsons across the street?

216
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:54,415
They're okay, right?

217
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:56,582
I'm sure your parents are okay too.

218
00:13:56,583 --> 00:13:57,666
You're right.

219
00:13:59,208 --> 00:14:00,833
I need to show you something.

220
00:14:13,125 --> 00:14:14,291
Is that a gun?

221
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:18,374
Jason, you can't buy a gun
and not tell me.

222
00:14:18,375 --> 00:14:20,415
- I was going to tell you.
- What about the kids?

223
00:14:20,416 --> 00:14:21,250
I know.

224
00:14:23,416 --> 00:14:26,582
- Okay, I've been having this nightmare.
- What? What nightmare?

225
00:14:26,583 --> 00:14:29,874
I woke up a couple weeks ago,
and I felt this thing.

226
00:14:29,875 --> 00:14:32,083
I just… I… I felt we weren't safe.

227
00:14:32,833 --> 00:14:34,125
And you feel safe now?

228
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,332
- I'm sorry.
- Okay.

229
00:14:37,333 --> 00:14:38,374
Okay?

230
00:14:38,375 --> 00:14:39,416
Okay.

231
00:14:44,250 --> 00:14:47,083
Show me how to use the stupid thing
before you put it back.

232
00:15:24,333 --> 00:15:25,665
Oh, come on.

233
00:15:25,666 --> 00:15:27,875
Come on.

234
00:15:29,708 --> 00:15:31,583
Good one, idiot.

235
00:16:06,750 --> 00:16:08,208
What the hell is this?

236
00:16:20,833 --> 00:16:22,125
Hey.

237
00:16:26,416 --> 00:16:27,791
I can't break through.

238
00:16:29,250 --> 00:16:33,625
The rain is creating some kind of barrier
around the house.

239
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:36,624
The same thing going down.

240
00:16:36,625 --> 00:16:38,207
Who's doing this?

241
00:16:38,208 --> 00:16:41,665
I don't know, but they've sealed us in.

242
00:16:41,666 --> 00:16:44,374
Are we gonna have to worry
about running out of air?

243
00:16:44,375 --> 00:16:45,916
I checked that too.

244
00:16:48,375 --> 00:16:49,540
Air is getting in.

245
00:16:49,541 --> 00:16:52,207
Okay. Then we wait for the rain to stop.

246
00:16:52,208 --> 00:16:53,375
Come to bed.

247
00:16:54,208 --> 00:16:55,291
Ann.

248
00:16:56,375 --> 00:16:59,208
Whatever is keeping us in here is not…

249
00:17:01,458 --> 00:17:02,666
man-made.

250
00:17:08,875 --> 00:17:10,875
Please hide this from the kids.

251
00:17:53,041 --> 00:17:54,041
Mm.

252
00:18:16,958 --> 00:18:18,166
I already tried it.

253
00:18:24,958 --> 00:18:26,790
