Half an apple?

506
00:33:18,416 --> 00:33:20,082
I already have this one.

507
00:33:20,083 --> 00:33:22,166
We were sort of hoping that you'd forget.

508
00:33:24,708 --> 00:33:25,624
What is this?

509
00:33:25,625 --> 00:33:27,915
Maybe you could use it
for a pretend hair salon.

510
00:33:27,916 --> 00:33:29,041
- Thanks.
- Okay.

511
00:33:29,666 --> 00:33:31,958
This is for both of you. Whoa, whoa, whoa!

512
00:33:33,041 --> 00:33:34,082
Piano books?

513
00:33:34,083 --> 00:33:37,874
Yeah, you know,
the piano that your grandma got you

514
00:33:37,875 --> 00:33:40,457
that's just been collecting dust.

515
00:33:40,458 --> 00:33:42,790
- But I don't wanna play piano.
- Okay.

516
00:33:42,791 --> 00:33:44,124
- Graham?
- No.

517
00:33:44,125 --> 00:33:45,374
- We tried.
- Awesome.

518
00:33:45,375 --> 00:33:47,583
Yeah. Gray, find a present for Mom.

519
00:33:48,083 --> 00:33:50,499
What? What did you get me?

520
00:33:50,500 --> 00:33:52,708
You guys, thank you.

521
00:33:57,083 --> 00:33:58,374
It's your very first tomato.

522
00:33:58,375 --> 00:34:01,124
They saw it growing in the kitchen,
and they wanted to surprise you.

523
00:34:01,125 --> 00:34:03,415
- You grew it, Mama.
- Oh my gosh.

524
00:34:03,416 --> 00:34:04,875
That's so sweet.

525
00:34:05,875 --> 00:34:08,207
Should I cut it so we can share it?

526
00:34:08,208 --> 00:34:11,500
- You can eat it all by yourself.
- Yeah, go ahead and eat your tomato.

527
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:23,332
It's really good.

528
00:34:23,333 --> 00:34:25,291
- I'm crying.
- Yeah.

529
00:34:37,791 --> 00:34:40,707
Mama! The old lady needs help!

530
00:34:40,708 --> 00:34:43,832
Mrs. Richardson. Take them to the den.

531
00:34:43,833 --> 00:34:44,915
- Dad.
- Let's go.

532
00:34:44,916 --> 00:34:45,915
What's happening? Dad?

533
00:34:45,916 --> 00:34:48,583
- Dad! No!
- Let's go. Come. Let's go. Go.

534
00:35:09,666 --> 00:35:11,333
Is she gonna be okay?

535
00:35:12,583 --> 00:35:14,833
No, honey. She was not okay.

536
00:35:19,541 --> 00:35:20,833
Is Christmas over yet?

537
00:35:23,666 --> 00:35:24,541
Yeah.

538
00:35:37,958 --> 00:35:39,000
That's the last of it.

539
00:35:39,958 --> 00:35:40,916
Sorry, Cass.

540
00:35:41,666 --> 00:35:43,666
Just hold it together for me.

541
00:36:00,083 --> 00:36:04,249
<i>Rain, rain, go away</i>

542
00:36:04,250 --> 00:36:07,582
<i>Come again another day</i>

543
00:36:07,583 --> 00:36:09,625
Don't worry, Cass.

544
00:36:30,750 --> 00:36:34,000
<i>Rain, rain, go</i>

545
00:36:34,875 --> 00:36:37,750
Please help me!

546
00:36:43,083 --> 00:36:45,040
What? What?

547
00:36:45,041 --> 00:36:48,457
There's a person outside. There she is!

548
00:36:48,458 --> 00:36:50,665
- What's wrong?
- Stay away from the window.

549
00:36:50,666 --> 00:36:51,666
Why?

550
00:36:56,458 --> 00:36:57,375
Mom! Dad!

551
00:36:59,166 --> 00:37:01,415
- Who is that?
- They're dead.

552
00:37:01,416 --> 00:37:03,791
It's the neighbor.

553
00:37:05,625 --> 00:37:08,375
They're dead. Everyone is dead!

554
00:37:09,416 --> 00:37:11,291
Don't let them see you!

555
00:37:11,833 --> 00:37:14,915
It's over.
They're here, and no help is coming.

556
00:37:14,916 --> 00:37:17,457
- Susan.
- No help is coming!

557
00:37:17,458 --> 00:37:20,249
- We can't help you. I'm sorry.
- Help me!

558
00:37:20,250 --> 00:37:22,458
You must… help!

559
00:37:26,791 --> 00:37:27,625
Hide.

560
00:38:04,625 --> 00:38:07,333
Okay, family meeting. Right now.

561
00:38:13,625 --> 00:38:16,790
- I don't know what I'm looking at.
- I've tried to tell you.

562
00:38:16,791 --> 00:38:18,915
But the one I saw seemed nice.

563
00:38:18,916 --> 00:38:21,207
Just… not like the ones tonight.

564
00:38:21,208 --> 00:38:22,916
Whatever we saw out there,

565
00:38:24,375 --> 00:38:28,041
whatever is keeping us in here,
it's… it's not nice.

566
00:38:34,041 --> 00:38:35,207
Listen to me.

567
00:38:35,208 --> 00:38:38,125
I'm not gonna let anything bad
happen to us.

568
00:38:41,083 --> 00:38:42,666
Can we sleep in your room tonight?

569
00:38:44,041 --> 00:38:45,000
Yeah.

570
00:38:52,541 --> 00:38:55,457
Let's limit
all signs of life visible from outside.

571
00:38:55,458 --> 00:38:58,915
- We start covering up all the windows.
- Especially when it's raining.

572
00:38:58,916 --> 00:39:00,833
Are monsters real?

573
00:39:01,833 --> 00:39:03,000
They are now.

574
00:39:03,541 --> 00:39:04,790
Not helpful, Gray.

575
00:39:04,791 --> 00:39:05,666
Sh.

576
00:39:06,416 --> 00:39:08,249
Let's settle down, okay?

577
00:39:08,250 --> 00:39:09,708
Okay, Mama.

578
00:39:11,125 --> 00:39:13,041
Sh. Go to bed.

579
00:39:22,291 --> 00:39:23,750
What do we do?

580
00:39:25,083 --> 00:39:26,375
We survive.

581
00:40:00,291 --> 00:40:03,457
Cassie? No. Drop it, Cassie!

582
00:40:03,458 --> 00:40:05,165
Hey! Hey.

583
00:40:05,166 --> 00:40:07,290
You know what?
You can play with Cassie later.

584
00:40:07,291 --> 00:40:09,166
Right now, let's do some PE time.

585
00:40:10,041 --> 00:40:13,875
Mom, Dad wants us to do PE, again.

586
00:40:51,041 --> 00:40:51,916
Dad!

587
00:40:54,625 --> 00:40:57,833
I think it's the chimney cap.
It must have fallen out.

588
00:40:59,833 --> 00:41:02,332
Yeah, you can see all the way through now.

589
00:41:02,333 --> 00:41:04,832
Can you see the cracks?
Are they getting bigger?

590
00:41:04,833 --> 00:41:06,915
Cracks?
Why do we have cracks in our chimney?

591
00:41:06,916 --> 00:41:08,540
'Cause our house has structural damage.

592
00:41:08,541 --> 00:41:11,124
Does that mean the house is
gonna fall on us?

593
00:41:11,125 --> 00:41:12,374
- I hope not.
- No.

594
00:41:12,375 --> 00:41:13,665
Guys, who cares?

595
00:41:13,666 --> 00:41:16,165
Maybe we can get out now
through the chimney.

596
00:41:16,166 --> 00:41:19,999
It's way too narrow at the top. My weight
would make the whole thing collapse, baby.

597
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:22,333
Then how does Santa get down the chimney?

598
00:41:25,708 --> 00:41:29,582
Guys, I'm kidding. Let me try going up.

599
00:41:29,583 --> 00:41:32,291
I'm the lightest,
so you can hoist me with my silks.

600
00:41:44,666 --> 00:41:45,750
I'll be fine.

601
00:41:46,333 --> 00:41:47,291
Step on it.

602
00:41:47,791 --> 00:41:49,082
Nice and slow, okay?

603
00:41:49,083 --> 00:41:50,666
- Bye, guys!
- No.

604
00:41:51,708 --> 00:41:52,916
Oh God.

605
00:41:53,583 --> 00:41:55,083
Okay. I don't like this.

606
00:41:59,500 --> 00:42:02,499
Wait, I can see the cracks!

607
00:42:02,500 --> 00:42:05,207
Don't touch them. Don't touch anything.

608
00:42:05,208 --> 00:42:08,040
You were right, Dad.
I could never get through here.

609
00:42:08,041 --> 00:42:10,040
Baby, I'm gonna bring you down, okay?

610
00:42:10,041 --> 00:42:11,957
Wait! I wanna try something.

611
00:42:11,958 --> 00:42:14,666
Just please be careful, okay?

612
00:42:16,708 --> 00:42:19,000
Careful! Slow down.

613
00:42:27,416 --> 00:42:29,583
My hand's outside the house!

614
00:42:30,125 --> 00:42:32,333
My hand's outside the house!

615
00:42:33,916 --> 00:42:35,874
My hand is outside the house!

616
00:42:35,875 --> 00:42:37,624
Mom, the weather's changing.

617
00:42:37,625 --> 00:42:39,457
I can feel the air and everything.

618
00:42:39,458 --> 00:42:42,457
Okay, that's enough.
Come down. Okay, bring her down now.

619
00:42:42,458 --> 00:42:45,291
- Careful, careful.
- Come on, come on.

620
00:42:48,583 --> 00:42:50,708
Take it slow. There we go.

621
00:42:51,666 --> 00:42:52,666
Almost there.

622
00:42:53,916 --> 00:42:55,124
Oh my gosh.

623
00:42:55,125 --> 00:42:56,707
- Good job. Are you okay?
- Yeah.

624
00:42:56,708 --> 00:42:59,625
Oh, my brave girl. I'm so proud of you.

625
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:04,000
What's with Cassidy?

626
00:43:04,500 --> 00:43:05,375
No.

627
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:16,416
Oh no.

628
00:43:18,458 --> 00:43:19,582
Cass.

629
00:43:19,583 --> 00:43:21,540
- No, don't move him.
- Sorry, Cass.

630
00:43:21,541 --> 00:43:24,291
- Oh, my Cass.
- It's his heart.

631
00:43:24,958 --> 00:43:27,125
- Aww.
- The medicine ran out.

632
00:43:29,166 --> 00:43:30,832
He had a really good life, you guys.

633
00:43:30,833 --> 00:43:34,750
- Why are you saying it like that?
- Because he's really old, honey.

634
00:43:36,125 --> 00:43:39,333
And sometimes when you get really old,
you can get very sick.

635
00:43:44,833 --> 00:43:48,582
Get the kids back to the den.
Put the TV on.

636
00:43:48,583 --> 00:43:51,832
Okay, you guys, come on.
Let's go watch <i>Annie</i> in the den.

637
00:43:51,833 --> 00:43:54,457
But, Mom, I wanna stay with Cassidy.

638
00:43:54,458 --> 00:43:55,500
I know.

639
00:44:02,916 --> 00:44:06,291
<i>So you've gotta hang on till tomorrow…</i>

640
00:44:07,500 --> 00:44:09,500
I know it's loud.
Cover your ears. Let's sing.

641
00:44:10,125 --> 00:44:12,374
<i>Tomorrow, tomorrow</i>

642
00:44:12,375 --> 00:44:14,000
<i>I love you</i>

643
00:44:28,500 --> 00:44:32,790
<i>You're only a day…</i>

644
00:44:32,791 --> 00:44:36,458
<i>Away</i>

645
00:44:51,208 --> 00:44:52,500
You did the right thing.

646
00:44:54,500 --> 00:44:55,500
Yeah.

647
00:44:57,666 --> 00:44:58,875
I have a problem now.

648
00:45:01,416 --> 00:45:03,166
He can't just stay here.

649
00:45:06,375 --> 00:45:07,749
The fireplace.

650
00:45:07,750 --> 00:45:12,249
Like, the… a cremation,
after the kids fall asleep?

651
00:45:12,250 --> 00:45:14,333
Yeah, it's an option.

652
00:45:16,083 --> 00:45:19,499
- But there is also the freezer.
- No, we're not doing that.

653
00:45:19,500 --> 00:45:25,333
If things get bad,
like, really, really bad…

654
00:45:27,791 --> 00:45:29,458
we might wish we had that option.

655
00:45:31,458 --> 00:45:33,416
I need you to handle it.

656
00:45:34,458 --> 00:45:38,125
And I don't wanna know anything about it.

657
00:45:50,125 --> 00:45:51,500
Okay. It's okay.

658
00:47:22,208 --> 00:47:25,083
Yeah. Yeah, come on.

659
00:47:32,041 --> 00:47:33,833
It's all right. You can take it.

660
00:47:35,333 --> 00:47:36,958
Yeah.

661
00:47:59,916 --> 00:48:01,958
What if doofus is right?

662
00:48:02,541 --> 00:48:04,291
Maybe they are aliens.

663
00:48:05,208 --> 00:48:07,040
Aliens can't control the rain.

664
00:48:07,041 --> 00:48:08,458
You don't know that.

665
00:48:14,041 --> 00:48:15,500
Whatever they are…

666
00:48:17,875 --> 00:48:19,208
we're their prisoners now.

667
00:48:19,916 --> 00:48:22,583
Why would they lock us inside forever?

668
00:48:23,708 --> 00:48:24,583
Why?

669
00:48:26,000 --> 00:48:27,708
Maybe to punish us.

670
00:48:36,541 --> 00:48:39,041
Guess that's all the sunlight
you get today.

671
00:48:44,041 --> 00:48:46,624
- Rain. Let's go.
- I got the den.

672
00:48:46,625 --> 00:48:49,208
Let's go. You know the drill.

673
00:48:54,666 --> 00:48:56,291
Let's go, Ru. Go.

674
00:48:59,833 --> 00:49:01,458
Ruth, come on.

675
00:49:02,375 --> 00:49:03,749
- Hey, what is this?
- What?

676
00:49:03,750 --> 00:49:05,332
- What's your problem?
- Okay, enough.

677
00:49:05,333 --> 00:49:07,124
Hey, don't do that.

678
00:49:07,125 --> 00:49:08,582
- Enough.
- Don't do that.

679
00:49:08,583 --> 00:49:09,708
Okay. Come on.

680
00:49:11,500 --> 00:49:12,499
My plant.

681
00:49:12,500 --> 00:49:14,124
- Hey. Hey.
- Get off.

682
00:49:14,125 --> 00:49:15,291
What are you doing?

683
00:49:20,875 --> 00:49:21,708
Don't!

684
00:49:39,500 --> 00:49:41,124
I just wanted to…

685
00:49:41,125 --> 00:49:44,832
It's okay. Hey, it's okay. It's gone.

686
00:49:44,833 --> 00:49:48,500
It's okay. You did good. You did good.
You all did real good.

687
00:50:02,875 --> 00:50:04,707
I'm still hungry.

688
00:50:04,708 --> 00:50:06,999
- We're rationing.
- I know, but I gotta eat.

689
00:50:07,000 --> 00:50:09,041
- So do I.
- Here.

690
00:50:12,000 --> 00:50:13,790
- Have the rest of mine.
- No!

691
00:50:13,791 --> 00:50:15,415
I want more than that.

692
00:50:15,416 --> 00:50:19,207
Just for tonight, please!
I'll go back to starving tomorrow.

693
00:50:19,208 --> 00:50:21,541
Stop it! Stop it right now!

694
00:50:23,333 --> 00:50:24,832
- Move!
- We're all hungry.

695
00:50:24,833 --> 00:50:26,124
- Let me see!
- I'm hungry too.

696
00:50:26,125 --> 00:50:27,707
Let me see in there, then I'll know.

697
00:50:27,708 --> 00:50:29,916
- I said no.
- Let her see.

698
00:50:41,666 --> 00:50:43,833
You wanna see it too? Fine.

699
00:51:00,916 --> 00:51:02,499
Mom! What's happening?

700
00:51:02,500 --> 00:51:04,666
She's fine. She's just…

701
00:51:14,625 --> 00:51:15,625
Okay.

702
00:51:19,583 --> 00:51:21,749
This is going to end one day.

703
00:51:21,750 --> 00:51:23,333
We'll survive this.

704
00:51:30,458 --> 00:51:31,790
No.

705
00:51:31,791 --> 00:51:34,915
It's not time for that anymore.

706
00:51:34,916 --> 00:51:36,624
It's time to be honest.

707
00:51:36,625 --> 00:51:38,457
- We're gonna starve.
- No. Stop.

708
00:51:38,458 --> 00:51:39,749
- Yes.
- No, don't say that.

709
00:51:39,750 --> 00:51:41,124
I refuse to watch our babies die.

710
00:51:41,125 --> 00:51:43,624
I'm not having this conversation with you.

711
00:51:43,625 --> 00:51:45,457
This is happening.

712
00:51:45,458 --> 00:51:47,374
No, we'll live.

713
00:51:47,375 --> 00:51:50,124
We'll do better than that. We'll thrive.

714
00:51:50,125 --> 00:51:51,666
I'll figure this out.

715
00:51:52,208 --> 00:51:53,208
Trust me.

716
00:51:54,291 --> 00:51:57,375
No. You won't.

717
00:51:58,666 --> 00:52:00,000
It's over.

718
00:52:10,708 --> 00:52:12,416
Mom, Dad.

719
00:52:13,000 --> 00:52:14,041
You could cook these.

720
00:52:17,541 --> 00:52:20,499
- Did I clean them wrong?
- No, you didn't do anything wrong, baby.

721
00:52:20,500 --> 00:52:21,541
Come here.

722
00:52:24,958 --> 00:52:26,791
Come here. You didn't do anything.

723
00:53:02,083 --> 00:53:03,291
Where are you going?

724
00:53:48,250 --> 00:53:49,250
Pull.

725
00:53:55,041 --> 00:53:56,582
What happens next?

726
00:53:56,583 --> 00:53:58,000
Now we wait.

727
00:54:01,250 --> 00:54:03,166
Sh. Sh.

728
00:54:04,791 --> 00:54:07,125
Yes. Go on, grab it.

729
00:54:09,041 --> 00:54:09,916
Yeah.

730
00:54:10,875 --> 00:54:12,583
Go, go. Oh.

731
00:54:21,250 --> 00:54:24,291
It's okay. It's all right.

732
00:54:45,833 --> 00:54:47,250
Pull!

733
00:55:13,750 --> 00:55:16,874
Oh no. No, no, no.
You should give it to the kids.

734
00:55:16,875 --> 00:55:19,332
You're cloudy headed.
You haven't eaten in days.

735
00:55:19,333 --> 00:55:22,791
Just eat and then go back to work.

736
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:13,290
Foxes eat carrots?

737
00:56:13,291 --> 00:56:15,166
This isn't for the fox.

738
00:56:36,541 --> 00:56:37,625
What's wrong?

739
00:57:01,250 --> 00:57:02,125
Chimney fishing.

740
00:57:02,833 --> 00:57:03,791
Chimney fishing.

741
00:57:06,333 --> 00:57:08,625
- Watch out, it's hot.
- Okay, go ahead.

742
00:57:21,208 --> 00:57:24,541
So, here. I need all of this pulled up.

743
00:57:26,333 --> 00:57:29,082
Once you get
beneath the underlayment and the subfloor,

744
00:57:29,083 --> 00:57:31,915
you're gonna get, like, a few inches
of soil and gonna hit the barrier.

745
00:57:31,916 --> 00:57:33,375
I'll make it work.

746
00:57:39,333 --> 00:57:41,333
<i>Days blurred into weeks,</i>

747
00:57:42,208 --> 00:57:44,166
<i>weeks into months.</i>

748
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:48,625
<i>People had no way of knowing
how long the visitors would be here,</i>

749
00:57:49,208 --> 00:57:51,916
<i>so they hid themselves to stay safe.</i>

750
00:57:54,166 --> 00:57:56,208
<i>Most people starved and died.</i>

751
00:57:57,166 --> 00:57:59,625
<i>Others lost hope and gave up.</i>

752
00:58:01,416 --> 00:58:04,791
<i>Still others found purpose and kept on.</i>

753
00:58:13,541 --> 00:58:16,916
<i>The lucky ones found togetherness.</i>

754
00:58:18,166 --> 00:58:19,499
I need more fertilizer.

755
00:58:19,500 --> 00:58:21,208
Damn, you know, I'm fresh out.

756
00:58:21,791 --> 00:58:23,291
We could make our own.

757
00:58:29,541 --> 00:58:31,499
What do you think?
I thought it was pretty good.

758
00:58:31,500 --> 00:58:32,666
Pretty good.

759
00:58:34,500 --> 00:58:35,458
Come on!

760
00:58:39,291 --> 00:58:40,666
I need more light.

761
00:58:47,125 --> 00:58:50,958
<i>The outside world
had become strange and dangerous.</i>

762
00:58:51,500 --> 00:58:55,875
<i>Inside, people found
what they needed to survive.</i>

763
00:58:59,458 --> 00:59:02,583
<i>Inside, they were free.</i>

764
00:59:12,666 --> 00:59:15,666
- How did they lose the gun?
- Yeah, I don't know, baby.

765
00:59:16,875 --> 00:59:19,125
<i>Ah! Ah!</i>

766
00:59:19,625 --> 00:59:22,333
<i>- Get off my plane!</i>
- Get off my plane!

767
00:59:23,708 --> 00:59:25,125
Yeah! Whoo!

768
00:59:25,916 --> 00:59:27,666
- Yeah!
- Whoo!

769
00:59:28,375 --> 00:59:29,666
Yeah!

770
00:59:34,000 --> 00:59:35,290
- What?
- No!

771
00:59:35,291 --> 00:59:36,832
Aw!

772
00:59:36,833 --> 00:59:39,249
We knew
this would happen eventually, right?

773
00:59:39,250 --> 00:59:42,250
Yeah, but there can still be music.

774
01:01:33,875 --> 01:01:34,875
Morning.

775
01:03:12,166 --> 01:03:13,166
Hello, rain.

776
01:03:15,375 --> 01:03:16,666
Right on time.

777
01:03:24,041 --> 01:03:26,582
What will it be for you today, sir?

778
01:03:26,583 --> 01:03:29,415
The usual, fade? Side and back?

779
01:03:29,416 --> 01:03:31,916
Oh, I didn't realize
you were entertaining.

780
01:03:32,833 --> 01:03:34,832
Hey, Graham.

781
01:03:34,833 --> 01:03:36,458
You ready for your next haircut?

782
01:03:49,375 --> 01:03:51,333
Wow, what's that?

783
01:03:52,041 --> 01:03:54,541
I hooked up the trap to be automatic.

784
01:03:57,541 --> 01:04:00,540
- So no more fishing.
- That's not real fishing, Ann.

785
01:04:00,541 --> 01:04:03,458
Aren't we growing enough food now
to stop using the traps?

786
01:05:09,375 --> 01:05:11,333
Ann?

787
01:05:11,916 --> 01:05:12,832
Hey, Ann?

788
01:05:12,833 --> 01:05:15,707
- The house is definitely sinking.
- House is sinking.

789
01:05:15,708 --> 01:05:18,624
That's great. That's, uh… lovely.
I wanna show you something.

790
01:05:18,625 --> 01:05:20,708
Okay, no, look. It's getting worse.

791
01:05:21,333 --> 01:05:24,540
Okay? The soil is eroding under the house.

792
01:05:24,541 --> 01:05:26,999
Yeah, five years of daily rain
will do that. Come on.

793
01:05:27,000 --> 01:05:30,457
It's like whatever's keeping us locked in
is the thing keeping the house together.

794
01:05:30,458 --> 01:05:32,790
I say just let it all fall apart.

795
01:05:32,791 --> 01:05:35,790
Maybe one day
we'll be all… living in an invisible box,

796
01:05:35,791 --> 01:05:39,000
and that can be kinda cool.
Call the kids. I wanna show you something.

797
01:05:42,625 --> 01:05:44,166
What?!

798
01:05:48,958 --> 01:05:50,874
What you gotta say about that, huh?

799
01:05:50,875 --> 01:05:52,582
- What?!
- Come on.

800
01:05:52,583 --> 01:05:53,999
Oh my God.

801
01:05:54,000 --> 01:05:55,124
- You hear that?
- Yeah.

802
01:05:55,125 --> 01:05:56,207
- Yeah?
- Yeah, I do.

803
01:05:56,208 --> 01:05:59,082
Nothing a little elbow grease
can't accomplish, am I right?

804
01:05:59,083 --> 01:06:01,082
Yeah. Yeah.

805
01:06:01,083 --> 01:06:03,332
Only got enough gas
to turn it on a few times.

806
01:06:03,333 --> 01:06:05,416
- Mm-hmm.
- She really runs.

807
01:06:06,208 --> 01:06:07,499
Right?

808
01:06:07,500 --> 01:06:09,499
I mean, come on.

809
01:06:09,500 --> 01:06:11,540
- Yeah.
- How many years?

810
01:06:11,541 --> 01:06:13,832
- Yeah, six.
- Seven.

811
01:06:13,833 --> 01:06:15,165
- Seven years!
- Give or take.

812
01:06:15,166 --> 01:06:17,957
Yeah, yeah, it's a lot of work.
Yeah, do you see this?

813
01:06:17,958 --> 01:06:19,374
Oh my God.

814
01:06:19,375 --> 01:06:20,832
Yeah, a lot of work.

815
01:06:20,833 --> 01:06:23,083
- It's a waste of time.
- What?

816
01:06:24,916 --> 01:06:26,333
What'd you… what'd you say?

817
01:06:28,041 --> 01:06:29,125
No, it…

818
01:06:30,541 --> 01:06:33,999
You built a car
that'll never drive anywhere, you know,

819
01:06:34,000 --> 01:06:35,165
so what would you call it?

820
01:06:35,166 --> 01:06:36,749
If you wanna work on something useful,

821
01:06:36,750 --> 01:06:39,165
you can help me put
the dew collector up tomorrow.

822
01:06:39,166 --> 01:06:41,790
Why? We already have all the food
and water that we need.

823
01:06:41,791 --> 01:06:44,333
We can't rely on that forever. Can we?

824
01:06:46,916 --> 01:06:48,291
You tell me. Can we rely on that?

825
01:06:49,458 --> 01:06:51,915
Power's gone. Gas is gone.

826
01:06:51,916 --> 01:06:53,125
Everything is gone.

827
01:06:53,708 --> 01:06:55,083
But we are still here.

828
01:06:56,333 --> 01:06:57,999
We are still here.

829
01:06:58,000 --> 01:06:59,415
I'm here. You're here.

830
01:06:59,416 --> 01:07:01,833
Your sister is here. Your mom is here.

831
01:07:02,708 --> 01:07:05,458
We survive because I fight for us.

832
01:07:08,166 --> 01:07:14,333
And if one day, Graham, this rain stops,
you bet I'm gonna be ready for it.

833
01:07:17,291 --> 01:07:19,500
Are you done showing us your stupid car?

834
01:07:22,041 --> 01:07:23,458
Yeah, Gray, I'm done.

835
01:07:25,375 --> 01:07:28,208
Graham, come on, wait. Graham, wait.

836
01:07:30,750 --> 01:07:32,166
<i>Graham's getting worse.</i>

837
01:07:32,666 --> 01:07:34,208
<i>They're both getting worse.</i>

838
01:07:35,041 --> 01:07:37,082
<i>This is not a childhood.</i>

839
01:07:37,083 --> 01:07:38,915
You think
I don't think about these things?

840
01:07:38,916 --> 01:07:41,166
You never talk about them.

841
01:07:41,708 --> 01:07:43,166
I have one job here.

842
01:07:43,666 --> 01:07:46,290
One job only,
which is to keep all of you guys alive.

843
01:07:46,291 --> 01:07:49,125
We are all in here with you too.

844
01:07:49,625 --> 01:07:52,375
This is not just your problem

845
01:07:53,041 --> 01:07:54,458
for you to fix.

846
01:07:55,458 --> 01:07:57,333
The kids miss their father.

847
01:07:58,416 --> 01:08:00,791
And I miss my husband.

848
01:08:13,375 --> 01:08:15,624
It's time to help
with the water collection.

849
01:08:15,625 --> 01:08:17,833
Shut the curtains. Let's go.

850
01:08:39,791 --> 01:08:43,125
Everybody's getting too lax
with the rules, especially you.

851
01:08:43,833 --> 01:08:44,874
- What?
- Yeah.

852
01:08:44,875 --> 01:08:48,332
We're too exposed from your drawings
in the attic, and that has to end.

853
01:08:48,333 --> 01:08:50,332
No, no, no.
You can't just take that from me.

854
01:08:50,333 --> 01:08:51,499
- I can.
- Are you kidding?

855
01:08:51,500 --> 01:08:52,582
- One mistake only…
- Mom?

856
01:08:52,583 --> 01:08:53,915
…and we risk losing everything.

857
01:08:53,916 --> 01:08:55,332
How long can we keep hiding?

858
01:08:55,333 --> 01:08:56,458
- Just--
- What's the point?

859
01:09:07,708 --> 01:09:09,916
Hide, hide, hide, hide!

860
01:09:11,166 --> 01:09:12,458
Okay.

861
01:09:20,958 --> 01:09:21,875
Go, go, go.

862
01:09:42,416 --> 01:09:43,708
Sh.

863
01:10:37,750 --> 01:10:39,290
Jason.

864
01:10:39,291 --> 01:10:40,791
The gun. Gun.

865
01:10:43,875 --> 01:10:44,750
I'll go.

866
01:10:45,333 --> 01:10:46,375
No. Stay there.

867
01:10:51,500 --> 01:10:52,416
Stay there.

868
01:11:25,583 --> 01:11:26,708
Ah!

869
01:11:40,541 --> 01:11:42,666
Graham! Graham! No!

870
01:11:43,791 --> 01:11:46,165
What are you doing?
Dad, what are you doing?

871
01:11:46,166 --> 01:11:48,165
Stop! Stop! Stop!

872
01:11:48,166 --> 01:11:50,582
I almost got out. I almost made it out.

873
01:11:50,583 --> 01:11:52,333
- I almost made it.
- Okay.

874
01:11:52,916 --> 01:11:55,000
- I could've…
- You okay?

875
01:11:59,000 --> 01:12:00,165
That's salt water.

876
01:12:00,166 --> 01:12:02,124
What? Hey.

877
01:12:02,125 --> 01:12:05,290
- You okay? No, wait.
- It's seawater.

878
01:12:05,291 --> 01:12:06,540
What?

879
01:12:06,541 --> 01:12:09,041
Come here, away from the window.

880
01:12:09,541 --> 01:12:11,125
Hey, hey, you guys hear that?

881
01:12:13,791 --> 01:12:15,000
The rain stopped.

882
01:12:58,583 --> 01:13:00,041
Leviathan.

883
01:13:00,958 --> 01:13:01,916
Kraken.

884
01:13:07,125 --> 01:13:08,250
Mermaids.

885
01:13:10,750 --> 01:13:12,374
Think about it, Dad.

886
01:13:12,375 --> 01:13:15,708
80% of the ocean floor is unexplored.

887
01:13:16,291 --> 01:13:19,540
What if these things aren't
from outer space?

888
01:13:19,541 --> 01:13:23,165
What if these tales of sea creatures
are real?

889
01:13:23,166 --> 01:13:25,707
What if that's why
they can control the rain?

890
01:13:25,708 --> 01:13:28,915
They're not conquering our world.
<i>This</i> is their world.

891
01:13:28,916 --> 01:13:30,124
It's their home.

892
01:13:30,125 --> 01:13:33,791
No, this is <i>our</i> home,
and you're safe here.

893
01:13:34,708 --> 01:13:35,916
I promise.

894
01:13:38,750 --> 01:13:39,916
If you say so.

895
01:13:41,125 --> 01:13:42,083
What…

896
01:13:42,583 --> 01:13:45,415
Why don't you… take a break from this?

897
01:13:45,416 --> 01:13:46,500
This…

898
01:13:47,083 --> 01:13:48,625
Go do something useful.

899
01:13:52,916 --> 01:13:53,875
Okay.

900
01:14:11,750 --> 01:14:13,083
Look at this.

901
01:14:14,208 --> 01:14:15,583
Everything's dying.

902
01:14:21,041 --> 01:14:23,540
Salt water. Ruthie was right.

903
01:14:23,541 --> 01:14:26,040
That thing came in here
and poisoned all the soil.

904
01:14:26,041 --> 01:14:29,124
It's the same with the drinking water.
We can't use any of it.

905
01:14:29,125 --> 01:14:32,415
So that's it, then.
They starve us out like everyone else.

906
01:14:32,416 --> 01:14:33,416
Ann.

907
01:14:38,208 --> 01:14:40,707
- They don't want us here, Jason.
- That's great.

908
01:14:40,708 --> 01:14:42,208
But where are we supposed to go?

909
01:14:48,541 --> 01:14:51,500
We have all new tarps for collecting dew,
so we'll do that.

910
01:14:52,125 --> 01:14:54,540
- We'll replant. We'll start over.
- You just said it yourself.

911
01:14:54,541 --> 01:14:56,582
- We don't have water.
- It's not raining now.

912
01:14:56,583 --> 01:14:58,582
- But it'll rain again.
- You have no idea.

913
01:14:58,583 --> 01:15:01,957
- This wasn't meant for you. Hey.
- We cannot replant.

914
01:15:01,958 --> 01:15:03,832
You're too small to be in that.

915
01:15:03,833 --> 01:15:06,957
What is it you keep telling us?
Three minutes without air.

916
01:15:06,958 --> 01:15:08,707
Three days without water.

917
01:15:08,708 --> 01:15:10,249
Three weeks without food.

918
01:15:10,250 --> 01:15:13,124
We have three days
before we die with no water.

919
01:15:13,125 --> 01:15:16,749
It's not gonna come to that.
We'll have enough water to survive.

920
01:15:16,750 --> 01:15:18,874
Just a little less than we used to.
I'll work it out.

921
01:15:18,875 --> 01:15:21,832
What happens when that thing
comes back here? What then?

922
01:15:21,833 --> 01:15:25,874
I don't know, Ann! I don't know!
What should I do? Shoot it?

923
01:15:25,875 --> 01:15:28,832
Open your eyes. You think
we're still alive because of you?

924
01:15:28,833 --> 01:15:30,957
We're still alive
because of a crack in the chimney.

925
01:15:30,958 --> 01:15:33,874
We're not better than anyone else
who died. We're just luckier!

926
01:15:33,875 --> 01:15:37,916
If we don't find a way out of this house,
we will die, and you know that!

927
01:15:44,458 --> 01:15:47,332
- Oh my God. I was trying to help.
- What is this?

928
01:15:47,333 --> 01:15:49,540
I don't know what happened.
I… I'm so sorry.

929
01:15:49,541 --> 01:15:51,375
I was trying to help. I didn't mean to…

930
01:15:52,833 --> 01:15:54,874
- Is it bad?
- Ruth, are you okay?

931
01:15:54,875 --> 01:15:56,040
Are you okay?

932
01:15:56,041 --> 01:15:58,374
- Ruth.
- No! Don't kill it.

933
01:15:58,375 --> 01:16:00,874
- What is going on?
- Wait. Let's get this cleaned up.

934
01:16:00,875 --> 01:16:03,499
- Hey, what's going on?
- I don't know. I'm sorry.

935
01:16:03,500 --> 01:16:05,625
- Dad, is she gonna be okay?
- Yeah.

936
01:16:08,791 --> 01:16:10,416
She's burning up.

937
01:16:11,333 --> 01:16:13,375
The infection is spreading.

938
01:16:14,041 --> 01:16:15,583
Her fever won't break.

939
01:16:16,125 --> 01:16:17,541
We have to do something.

940
01:16:20,625 --> 01:16:23,541
This is the last of our water.
She needs it.

941
01:16:27,291 --> 01:16:28,958
Hey.

942
01:16:29,875 --> 01:16:30,832
Easy.

943
01:16:30,833 --> 01:16:32,416
We need antibiotics.

944
01:18:08,166 --> 01:18:09,916
Jason!

945
01:18:10,416 --> 01:18:14,041
Jason! Jason!

946
01:18:24,833 --> 01:18:28,541
Jason!

947
01:18:30,208 --> 01:18:31,875
Graham! Help!

948
01:18:34,916 --> 01:18:36,166
Come on. Come on.

949
01:18:38,291 --> 01:18:39,958
Cracks. The cracks.

950
01:18:43,041 --> 01:18:44,041
What are you doing?

951
01:18:54,833 --> 01:18:56,500
The house is sinking.

952
01:19:00,958 --> 01:19:03,207
Look at that. Look. The crack.

953
01:19:03,208 --> 01:19:04,083
Jason!

954
01:19:04,666 --> 01:19:06,124
The barrier isn't deep.

955
01:19:06,125 --> 01:19:08,457
- See?
- Jason, talk to me.

956
01:19:08,458 --> 01:19:09,874
- See?
- What do you see?

957
01:19:09,875 --> 01:19:11,790
- It shifted.
- Jason.

958
01:19:11,791 --> 01:19:13,249
- Let me try.
- What?

959
01:19:13,250 --> 01:19:15,375
I can find a way out.
I can find a way out.

960
01:19:17,541 --> 01:19:19,082
Stop. Hey.

961
01:19:19,083 --> 01:19:21,040
Yes, it's deeper. There.

962
01:19:21,041 --> 01:19:23,332
Look at me. Look at me. Jason.

963
01:19:23,333 --> 01:19:25,249
- No. You listen to me.
- That's enough.

964
01:19:25,250 --> 01:19:26,540
You said the house was sinking.

965
01:19:26,541 --> 01:19:27,790
- Stop.
- Remember?

966
01:19:27,791 --> 01:19:31,124
- Stop for a second.
- Maybe something else is shifting.

967
01:19:31,125 --> 01:19:33,582
- You need to take a breath.
- Like the cracks in the chimney.

968
01:19:33,583 --> 01:19:36,290
I have to try and find it. Find it.

969
01:19:36,291 --> 01:19:37,375
Find what?

970
01:19:38,666 --> 01:19:40,790
- See?
- See what?

971
01:19:40,791 --> 01:19:42,541
See? Follow the crack.

972
01:19:43,041 --> 01:19:44,499
- The crack is our escape.
- No!

973
01:19:44,500 --> 01:19:48,249
We have to follow the cracks.
I just have to find where the crack goes.

974
01:19:48,250 --> 01:19:49,915
What are you doing? Stop.

975
01:19:49,916 --> 01:19:52,290
- Stop it, Jason!
- I can do it!

976
01:19:52,291 --> 01:19:53,707
Stop! Let me try!

977
01:19:53,708 --> 01:19:55,124
I have to!

978
01:19:55,125 --> 01:19:56,249
That's enough!

979
01:19:56,250 --> 01:19:58,125
Enough!

980
01:19:59,291 --> 01:20:01,082
- You have to…
- No!

981
01:20:01,083 --> 01:20:03,250
Stop!

982
01:20:24,208 --> 01:20:25,583
It went through.

983
01:20:27,541 --> 01:20:29,916
Stand back! Stand back!

984
01:20:39,833 --> 01:20:41,124
Help me.

985
01:20:41,125 --> 01:20:42,333
Here.

986
01:20:55,125 --> 01:20:58,332
- Where does it go?
- It leads to the main sewer pipe.

987
01:20:58,333 --> 01:21:00,625
The whole neighborhood is connected.

988
01:21:01,291 --> 01:21:03,083
The Richardsons.

989
01:21:05,333 --> 01:21:06,874
He's the dentist.

990
01:21:06,875 --> 01:21:08,665
- He has antibiotics.
- Yeah.

991
01:21:08,666 --> 01:21:10,749
- I just have to get in here.
- You won't fit.

992
01:21:10,750 --> 01:21:13,707
- I just have to make this bigger.
- Jason, the pipe's metal.

993
01:21:13,708 --> 01:21:17,000
- I have to try.
- We don't have time. We don't have time.

994
01:21:17,708 --> 01:21:18,790
I can fit now.

995
01:21:18,791 --> 01:21:21,665
No. No, no, no.

996
01:21:21,666 --> 01:21:23,041
This one is me.

997
01:21:25,000 --> 01:21:26,625
This one's me.

998
01:21:33,083 --> 01:21:35,458
- Testing, testing.
- Loud and clear.

999
01:21:39,041 --> 01:21:40,707
You know what I was thinking?

1000
01:21:40,708 --> 01:21:45,833
That "never put your wife down the toilet"
should have been one of my wedding vows.

1001
01:21:46,416 --> 01:21:49,208
It's a little late for that.
Don't you think?

1002
01:21:50,500 --> 01:21:51,583
Be careful, please.

1003
01:21:52,208 --> 01:21:53,333
I will.

1004
01:21:54,750 --> 01:21:57,125
And I'm bringing back medicine
for our baby.

1005
01:22:07,875 --> 01:22:08,916
Okay.

1006
01:22:11,416 --> 01:22:13,375
Go.

1007
01:22:22,041 --> 01:22:23,166
Ready.

1008
01:22:39,750 --> 01:22:41,583
Ann, can you see anything?

1009
01:22:45,041 --> 01:22:45,875
<i>Nothing.</i>

1010
01:22:50,750 --> 01:22:52,208
I'm gonna keep going.

1011
01:23:22,125 --> 01:23:23,207
Wait.

1012
01:23:23,208 --> 01:23:24,374
<i>There's a loose brick.</i>

1013
01:23:24,375 --> 01:23:26,833
Okay, Ann, you should come back.
Come back.

1014
01:23:31,458 --> 01:23:33,791
- Mom?
- Ann? Ann?

1015
01:23:34,500 --> 01:23:37,249
- No. Please, no.
- Mom, can you hear me?

1016
01:23:37,250 --> 01:23:38,374
Oh no, oh no.

1017
01:23:38,375 --> 01:23:39,708
Mom! Mom, come back!

1018
01:23:42,458 --> 01:23:43,291
Ann!

1019
01:23:55,583 --> 01:23:57,582
Dad! Come here right now!

1020
01:23:57,583 --> 01:24:00,291
Hurry up! Dad, come here.

1021
01:24:01,458 --> 01:24:03,416
Look, look. Come here. Hurry up.

1022
01:24:04,083 --> 01:24:07,082
- Look. Look. She made it.
- <i>Can you hear me? Hello?</i>

1023
01:24:07,083 --> 01:24:09,207
<i>Hey, can you hear me?</i>

1024
01:24:09,208 --> 01:24:11,040
- Yeah.
- Mom, Mom, are you okay?

1025
01:24:11,041 --> 01:24:12,791
<i>Yeah, I'm okay.</i>

1026
01:24:21,250 --> 01:24:22,500
It's Mrs. Richardson.

1027
01:24:29,583 --> 01:24:31,041
The tide came in?

1028
01:24:31,625 --> 01:24:34,625
It's like the whole house was flooded
for years.

1029
01:24:40,458 --> 01:24:42,082
We've run out of time, babe.

1030
01:24:42,083 --> 01:24:45,375
- <i>Mom, it's starting to rain.</i>
- <i>Ann, it's raining.</i>

1031
01:24:57,041 --> 01:24:59,707
Ann, find it and get out now!

1032
01:24:59,708 --> 01:25:01,374
I'm not leaving without it.

1033
01:25:01,375 --> 01:25:04,291
<i>It's too late. Ann! The rain is here.</i>

1034
01:25:04,958 --> 01:25:06,000
Hold on.

1035
01:25:07,166 --> 01:25:08,541
Mr. Richardson?

1036
01:25:09,041 --> 01:25:10,540
Uh! Yes!

1037
01:25:10,541 --> 01:25:12,750
- <i>What?</i>
- Yes.

1038
01:25:13,291 --> 01:25:14,790
Okay. Okay.

1039
01:25:14,791 --> 01:25:16,375
Clindacyclin.

1040
01:25:17,083 --> 01:25:18,874
- Azithromycin.
- <i>What is that?</i>

1041
01:25:18,875 --> 01:25:20,374
- <i>Antibiotics.</i>
- Tetracycline.

1042
01:25:20,375 --> 01:25:22,124
- <i>Antibiotics!</i>
- Penicillin.

1043
01:25:22,125 --> 01:25:23,500
<i>Okay, Ann, run! Run!</i>

1044
01:25:24,083 --> 01:25:26,082
- Look!
- <i>Get out of there! Now! Come on!</i>

1045
01:25:26,083 --> 01:25:27,832
- Go! Come on!
- Go!

1046
01:25:27,833 --> 01:25:31,458
- Look! I got it!
- <i>Go! Go now! Go!</i>

1047
01:25:56,750 --> 01:25:58,041
Ah, no.

1048
01:26:45,875 --> 01:26:47,249
I'm down here!

1049
01:26:47,250 --> 01:26:50,374
I'm here! Come on.
Throw me the silk! Bring me up now!

1050
01:26:50,375 --> 01:26:51,750
Here, grab it.

1051
01:27:23,250 --> 01:27:24,125
You got this.

1052
01:27:42,708 --> 01:27:45,582
Here you go. Okay.
Open your mouth. Here you go.

1053
01:27:45,583 --> 01:27:47,624
We got the meds, okay?

1054
01:27:47,625 --> 01:27:50,583
Open and take it. Okay, open the water.

1055
01:27:51,250 --> 01:27:52,708
Good. There you go.

1056
01:27:53,666 --> 01:27:55,375
These should kick in fast.

1057
01:27:56,083 --> 01:27:57,707
You're gonna be okay.

1058
01:27:57,708 --> 01:27:59,749
That's my girl. Come on.

1059
01:27:59,750 --> 01:28:00,791
Okay.

1060
01:28:01,458 --> 01:28:02,458
Okay.

1061
01:28:03,250 --> 01:28:05,250
Ann, where's the gun?

1062
01:28:06,708 --> 01:28:07,708
I lost it.

1063
01:28:32,833 --> 01:28:35,000
It is going to be coming for us now.

1064
01:28:35,875 --> 01:28:38,457
It doesn't know how many of us there are.

1065
01:28:38,458 --> 01:28:40,666
You take the kids to the attic

1066
01:28:41,291 --> 01:28:42,374
and hide.

1067
01:28:42,375 --> 01:28:43,750
I'll stay here.

1068
01:28:45,083 --> 01:28:46,208
And, Ann,

1069
01:28:47,166 --> 01:28:48,916
no matter what you hear,

1070
01:28:49,583 --> 01:28:50,666
please

1071
01:28:52,125 --> 01:28:53,915
don't come out until the rain stops.

1072
01:28:53,916 --> 01:28:56,666
- You're giving up.
- This is the opposite of giving up. I'm…

1073
01:28:57,166 --> 01:29:00,499
You are going to live. All of you.

1074
01:29:00,500 --> 01:29:01,958
And you're gonna live for me.

1075
01:29:03,041 --> 01:29:06,125
This isn't living, surviving.

1076
01:29:06,916 --> 01:29:08,541
It's just not enough anymore.

1077
01:29:09,666 --> 01:29:12,165
We know that they can open that door,

1078
01:29:12,166 --> 01:29:14,457
and if they can come in,
then we can get out.

1079
01:29:14,458 --> 01:29:15,957
We'll fight them if we have to.

1080
01:29:15,958 --> 01:29:19,124
We can't fight them.
You don't know what you're talking about.

1081
01:29:19,125 --> 01:29:22,249
If there's even the slightest chance
that we can escape,

1082
01:29:22,250 --> 01:29:23,832
I'm taking that chance.

1083
01:29:23,833 --> 01:29:24,916
He's right.

1084
01:29:25,875 --> 01:29:29,208
Our family is breaking apart
trying to survive.

1085
01:29:29,916 --> 01:29:32,125
There's no life left here for us.

1086
01:29:33,333 --> 01:29:34,666
We have to try.

1087
01:29:36,875 --> 01:29:40,375
We have to escape, no matter the cost.

1088
01:29:43,125 --> 01:29:47,333
Okay. We'll do it together,
and we use what we have.

1089
01:29:47,916 --> 01:29:49,333
What do we have?

1090
01:29:50,250 --> 01:29:51,333
Our house.

1091
01:29:52,041 --> 01:29:54,374
<i>Open up the windows.</i>

1092
01:29:54,375 --> 01:29:55,791
<i>We're done hiding.</i>

1093
01:29:56,333 --> 01:29:57,541
<i>We're gonna let them come in.</i>

1094
01:29:59,625 --> 01:30:03,166
<i>We will do whatever it takes
to get out of here.</i>

1095
01:30:11,083 --> 01:30:13,458
Hey. Can you take this?

1096
01:30:27,541 --> 01:30:29,875
<i>Now we are going to trap them.</i>

1097
01:30:30,375 --> 01:30:32,500
<i>Graham, you'll track the creature.</i>

1098
01:30:33,000 --> 01:30:35,041
<i>Ruth, you cast the line.</i>

1099
01:30:36,541 --> 01:30:40,416
<i>Ann, you lure it to me,
and I'll set the hook.</i>

1100
01:30:40,916 --> 01:30:44,083
<i>We'll reel it in, then make our escape.</i>

1101
01:30:47,333 --> 01:30:50,541
<i>They trapped us in here,
thinking it would kill us.</i>

1102
01:30:54,125 --> 01:30:57,916
<i>Today is our last day in this house.</i>

1103
01:30:59,458 --> 01:31:01,041
<i>Let's go fishing.</i>

1104
01:31:25,458 --> 01:31:26,333
Be safe.

1105
01:32:38,500 --> 01:32:39,708
Ah! Ah!

1106
01:32:56,041 --> 01:32:57,416
Ah! Ah!

1107
01:32:58,291 --> 01:33:00,040
Ruth!

1108
01:33:00,041 --> 01:33:01,375
- Are you okay?
- Yeah!

1109
01:33:04,416 --> 01:33:05,416
Graham!

1110
01:33:08,416 --> 01:33:09,333
Where's Dad?

1111
01:33:11,125 --> 01:33:13,375
- Jason!
- I'm okay!

1112
01:33:18,250 --> 01:33:19,500
Ah!

1113
01:33:32,750 --> 01:33:33,916
It's here!

1114
01:33:34,583 --> 01:33:36,000
Where's it coming from?

1115
01:33:37,625 --> 01:33:38,791
It's gone!

1116
01:33:39,958 --> 01:33:40,958
Come on.

1117
01:33:43,083 --> 01:33:44,540
It got inside!

1118
01:33:44,541 --> 01:33:47,290
Mom, hide! It's in the house!

1119
01:33:47,291 --> 01:33:49,583
Dad! It's coming towards you!

1120
01:34:05,125 --> 01:34:06,041
Where are you?

1121
01:34:09,125 --> 01:34:10,457
I don't have a shot!

1122
01:34:10,458 --> 01:34:12,957
Ann! Light it up!

1123
01:34:12,958 --> 01:34:14,166
Light it up now!

1124
01:34:24,583 --> 01:34:25,541
It's coming back!

1125
01:34:26,708 --> 01:34:28,000
Come on.

1126
01:34:34,333 --> 01:34:36,416
Ah! Ah! Ah!

1127
01:34:38,000 --> 01:34:39,375
Gotcha.

1128
01:34:44,416 --> 01:34:45,791
- Ah!
- Dad!

1129
01:34:53,291 --> 01:34:54,708
- Dad!
- No!

1130
01:34:59,958 --> 01:35:01,625
- Jason!
- Dad!

1131
01:35:02,916 --> 01:35:04,041
Jason!

1132
01:35:07,416 --> 01:35:08,916
Ah! Ah!

1133
01:35:09,791 --> 01:35:11,540
We gotta go! Come on!

1134
01:35:11,541 --> 01:35:13,040
Come on, Dad! Come on!

1135
01:35:13,041 --> 01:35:15,541
Hurry up! Let's go! Let's go!

1136
01:35:19,291 --> 01:35:22,457
The water is rising too fast!
We have to get to the attic!

1137
01:35:22,458 --> 01:35:23,665
Where's the harpoon?

1138
01:35:23,666 --> 01:35:25,333
I missed. It's in the kitchen.

1139
01:35:27,750 --> 01:35:29,540
Forget it. Let's go!

1140
01:35:29,541 --> 01:35:31,290
I can get it!

1141
01:35:31,291 --> 01:35:32,750
I'll meet you up there.

1142
01:35:35,625 --> 01:35:36,458
Go.

1143
01:36:58,375 --> 01:36:59,333
Watch out!

1144
01:36:59,958 --> 01:37:01,750
Hurry! Go!

1145
01:37:02,250 --> 01:37:03,957
- Hurry!
- Go!

1146
01:37:03,958 --> 01:37:05,625
Come on! Go!

1147
01:37:06,666 --> 01:37:08,166
- Come on!
- Run!

1148
01:37:09,708 --> 01:37:11,125
Come on!

1149
01:37:11,666 --> 01:37:14,082
Ruth, try the window. Dad!

1150
01:37:14,083 --> 01:37:15,875
Come on! Push!

1151
01:37:20,416 --> 01:37:22,541
- Come on!
- The hook, the hook!

1152
01:37:25,000 --> 01:37:27,499
Come on, let's go. I'm okay. I'm okay.

1153
01:37:27,500 --> 01:37:28,790
We have nowhere to go.

1154
01:37:28,791 --> 01:37:30,415
- You get this loaded!
- Okay.

1155
01:37:30,416 --> 01:37:31,416
Quick!

1156
01:37:35,125 --> 01:37:36,415
There you go.

1157
01:37:36,416 --> 01:37:38,125
- Ah!
- Ah!

1158
01:37:41,083 --> 01:37:43,415
Ruth, cast the line!

1159
01:37:43,416 --> 01:37:44,666
We need to find the silk!

1160
01:37:56,208 --> 01:37:57,582
It's too dark!

1161
01:37:57,583 --> 01:37:59,082
Just stay together!

1162
01:37:59,083 --> 01:38:01,041
Breathe! Take a deep breath!

1163
01:39:10,875 --> 01:39:12,374
I can't hold on!

1164
01:39:12,375 --> 01:39:13,333
Graham!

1165
01:39:32,041 --> 01:39:33,375
Go! Hurry!

1166
01:39:44,083 --> 01:39:46,750
Open the door, or I'm gonna gut you!

1167
01:39:51,375 --> 01:39:53,457
Jason, the house is coming down!

1168
01:39:53,458 --> 01:39:54,458
Let us out!

1169
01:39:59,625 --> 01:40:01,166
It's not opening.

1170
01:40:02,208 --> 01:40:04,124
Open the door!

1171
01:40:04,125 --> 01:40:05,332
Dad, stop!

1172
01:40:05,333 --> 01:40:07,833
If you kill it, we'll never get out!

1173
01:40:12,916 --> 01:40:16,374
I tried to tell you,
but the one I saw seemed nice.

1174
01:40:16,375 --> 01:40:19,082
- It's not nice.
- <i>She's trying to communicate.</i>

1175
01:40:19,083 --> 01:40:21,375
- This is their home.
- No, this is <i>our</i> home.

1176
01:40:26,291 --> 01:40:28,957
I have one job only,
which is to keep all of you guys alive.

1177
01:40:28,958 --> 01:40:31,207
This is not just your problem.

1178
01:40:31,208 --> 01:40:33,040
We survive because I fight for us.

1179
01:40:33,041 --> 01:40:36,665
You bought a gun?
What do we do when that thing comes back?

1180
01:40:36,666 --> 01:40:37,999
I don't know! Shoot it?

1181
01:40:38,000 --> 01:40:39,458
No, no, no! Don't kill it!

1182
01:41:42,666 --> 01:41:44,124
Mom, Dad?!

1183
01:41:44,125 --> 01:41:45,291
It's okay.

1184
01:42:38,250 --> 01:42:39,250
Ruth!

1185
01:42:42,416 --> 01:42:43,707
Ruth!

1186
01:42:43,708 --> 01:42:44,708
Stop!

1187
01:42:48,000 --> 01:42:50,083
Ruth! Ruth, stop!

1188
01:43:01,458 --> 01:43:04,666
<i>Everyone remembers where they were
the day the rain stopped.</i>

1189
01:43:06,291 --> 01:43:09,458
<i>It was a Tuesday, not quite summer.</i>

1190
01:43:13,583 --> 01:43:15,915
<i>For the first time in years,</i>

1191
01:43:15,916 --> 01:43:18,416
<i>my family felt hope.</i>

1192
01:43:20,250 --> 01:43:24,458
<i>In the end, an act of mercy set us free.</i>

1193
01:43:25,166 --> 01:43:29,291
<i>We showed it to them,
and they showed it to us.</i>

1194
01:43:32,291 --> 01:43:36,790
<i>We never saw them again,
but we think they're still out there.</i>

1195
01:43:36,791 --> 01:43:39,708
<i>After all, it's their home too.</i>

1196
01:43:44,000 --> 01:43:45,000
Where to?

1197
01:43:50,958 --> 01:43:52,125
Sheet the mainsail!

1198
01:43:55,500 --> 01:44:00,083
<i>My parents, my brother, and I
set off in search of a new home.</i>

1199
01:44:05,375 --> 01:44:08,750
{\an8}<i>For many years,
we felt like we were alone.</i>

1200
01:44:11,916 --> 01:44:13,250
<i>After the rain,</i>

1201
01:44:14,291 --> 01:44:16,583
<i>we knew we didn't have to be.</i>

1202
01:44:17,208 --> 01:44:18,750
<i>Can anybody hear me?</i>

1203
01:44:19,583 --> 01:44:22,125
<i>Are there any other survivors out there?</i>

1204
01:44:26,000 --> 01:44:27,208
<i>Hello?</i>

